      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:1:3:12",
      "text": [
        " الْبَنُونَ نَعِيمٌ وَ الْبَنَاتُ حَسَنَاتٌ وَ اللَّهُ يَسْأَلُ عَنِ النَّعِيمِ وَ يُثِيبُ عَلَى الْحَسَنَاتِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "A number of our companions, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Al Husayn Bin Musa, from Ahmad Bin Al Fazl, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The sons are Bounties, and the daughters are blessings, and Allah<sup>azwj</sup> would Question about the Bounties but He<sup>azwj</sup> would Rewards upon the ‘حَسَنَاتٌ’ (blessings)."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "12. A number of our people have narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from al-Husayn ibn Musa from Ahmad ibn al-Fadl who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘Sons are bounties and daughters are good deeds, Allah questions one about the bounties but for the good deeds He gives good rewards.”’ "
        ]
      }
    },
